{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","externalID":"s:9Traversal27EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEventO","title":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"EdgeSearchEvents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/EdgeSearchEvents.swift#L14"},"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each source is discovered first. Then, for each vertex in the order discovered, its out-edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are reported as tree edges (to an undiscovered vertex, which is then discovered) or non-tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges (to a discovered one); then the vertex is finished. In a directed graph every out-edge of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"ty